 r←Test_AskNumber_005(stopFlag batchFlag);parms;msg;was;⎕TRAP
⍝ Exercise the "OnOkay" callback with all possible ways to define it.
 r←∆Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP'
 #.TEMP←⎕NS''
 ⎕THIS.Result←¯1
 #.TEMP.MyCallback←{
     n←⍵
     ⎕THIS.Result←1
     0<n.Input.Value:1
     ⎕THIS.Result←0
     0
 }
 #.TEMP.parms←#._APLGUI.GUI.Request.CreateParmsForNumber
 #.TEMP.parms.timeout←0.1
 #.TEMP.parms.default←1
 #.TEMP.parms.onOkay←'#.TEMP.MyCallback'

 {}#.TEMP.parms #._APLGUI.GUI.Request.AskForNumber'Number of copies:'
 →FailsIf 1≠#.TEMP.Result
 #.TEMP.(⎕EX ⎕NL 2)

 ⎕THIS.Result←¯1
 #.TEMP.parms.onOkay←#.TEMP'MyCallback'
 {}#.TEMP.parms #._APLGUI.GUI.Request.AskForNumber'Number of copies:'
 →FailsIf 1≠#.TEMP.Result
 #.TEMP.(⎕EX ⎕NL 2)

 ⎕THIS.Result←¯1
 #.TEMP.parms.onOkay←'MyCallback'
 was←⎕CS #.TEMP
 parms←#._APLGUI.GUI.Request.CreateParmsForNumber
 parms.default←3
 parms.timeout←0.1
 parms.onOkay←'#.TEMP.MyCallback'
 {}parms #._APLGUI.GUI.Request.AskForNumber'Number of copies:'
 ⎕CS was
 →FailsIf 1≠#.TEMP.Result

 r←∆OK
